Monolayer BN - MF/Epsilon_q
===========================

In this directory we perform a non-self-consistent (NSCF) mean-field
calculation to generate the occupied Bloch states with a small q-shift needed
to construct the dielectric matrix at a small q-vector. The resulting
wavefunction file will be read as WFNq by the Epsilon code.


Instructions
------------

  1. Take a look at the input file ``kgrid.inp`` for ``k-grid.x``. Note the small
     q-shift.

  2. Run ``./01-get_kgrid.sh`` to generate the k-grid. Take a look at the
     output ``kgrid.out`` and the log ``kgrid.log``. How many points does the reduced
     shifted grid have? How does that compare with the number of points on
     the original uniform grid?

  3. Verify that the k-points in the Octopus input file ``inp`` are the same as
     those in ``kgrid.out``.

  4. Run ``./02-calculate_wfn.qsub`` to calculate the wavefunctions using
     Octopus. This should take about 2 mins.
